messages.content:
{
  "message": "I’m on it. Since you’re abroad, we’ll tackle both your account settings (roaming, data limits) and your phone’s settings. Here’s my plan and why: 1) Verify your line is roaming-enabled and that you haven’t hit a data cap—both would stop or slow data while abroad. 2) Optimize phone settings (mobile data/roaming toggles, network mode, Data Saver/VPN, APN) to target Excellent speed. First I need to identify your account to check and enable roaming if needed. Please provide: • The phone number on the affected line (with country code if possible). • Your current city in France (helps understand local conditions). • Can you make/receive calls and regular texts right now? While I pull up your line, please do these quick checks on your phone and share the results: 1) Status snapshot: Open your status bar and tell me what you see for: signal bars, network type (5G/4G/3G/2G), and whether a roaming “R” shows. 2) Mobile data and roaming: Ensure Mobile Data is ON and Data Roaming is ON in Settings. 3) Data Saver: If Data Saver is ON, turn it OFF. 4) VPN: If a VPN is connected, disconnect it for now. 5) Network mode: Set preferred network to 4G/5G (not 2G/3G). 6) Quick reset: Toggle Airplane Mode ON for 10 seconds, then OFF. After that, please run a quick speed test and tell me the result. Our goal is “Excellent.” Once you send your phone number, I’ll immediately: • Check if your line’s roaming is enabled; if not, I’ll enable it at no cost. • Check your data usage versus plan limit; if you’re capped, we can refuel up to 2GB or discuss a plan change to restore fast data. If any settings were changed, I may have you reboot the phone to apply them. Please share your phone number and the quick-check results, and we’ll get you to Excellent speed if the local network allows it."
}

