      "step": "Messaging app permissions",
      "how": "Settings > Apps > Messaging > Permissions.",
      "tell_me": "Does it have Storage/Photos and SMS permissions?",
      "why": "MMS needs access to media and SMS functions."
    }
  ],
  "what_i_will_check_on_my_side_after_identification": [
    "Line status (must be Active; if Suspended, we’ll resolve the cause).",
    "Current billing-cycle data usage vs plan limit (if you’re out of data, MMS will fail; we can add up to 2 GB or discuss plan changes).",
    "Roaming enablement on your line if you are traveling (I can enable it for you at no cost if needed)."
  ],
  "next_steps": [
    "Please reply with your identifier (phone number/Customer ID or full name + DOB) and the answers/results from the quick checks.",
    "Based on that, I’ll guide you through any needed fixes (e.g., turn off Airplane mode, enable mobile data, switch to 4G/5G preferred, temporarily disable Wi‑Fi Calling, reset APN to default and reboot, grant messaging app permissions)."
  ]
}

