{
  "thought_process": "I’m going to troubleshoot both possible causes: (1) on-device settings/issues like Airplane Mode, SIM problems, or network settings, and (2) account/line issues such as a suspended line. To check the line status, I need to identify your account. In parallel, I’ll have you run two quick checks on your phone to pinpoint the cause.",
  "request": {
    "customer_identification": "Please provide one of the following so I can look up your line and check for any suspension or account issues:",
    "accepted_identifiers": [
      "The phone number of the affected line (preferred)",
      "OR your full name AND date of birth (YYYY-MM-DD)",
      "OR your customer ID"
    ]
  },
  "questions": [
    "Are you currently traveling outside your usual/home area (possibly roaming)?",
    "Did anything change recently (new phone/SIM/eSIM transfer, plan change, or APN/settings changes)?",
    "Is this happening everywhere you go or only in a specific location?"
  ],
  "steps_for_you": [
    "On your phone, run check_status_bar and tell me exactly what it shows (Airplane Mode, signal strength icon like 📵/📶, network type 5G/4G/etc., and whether mobile data shows as enabled/disabled).",
    "Then run check_network_status and share the results (airplane mode status, signal strength none/poor/fair/good/excellent, network type, mobile data ON/OFF, and data roaming ON/OFF)."
  ],
  "next_actions_after_you_reply": "With your identifier, I’ll check your line status on our side. With the status bar and network check results, I’ll guide you through precise fixes (turning off Airplane Mode, reseating SIM if needed, resetting APN, or adjusting network mode). If the line is suspended due to billing, I’ll help resolve that right away and restore service."
}

