messages.content:
{
  "thought_process": "Your phone shows two device-side blockers: Airplane Mode is ON (which disables all cellular radios) and the SIM is locked with a PIN (which prevents network registration). We’ll first turn Airplane Mode OFF, then unlock the SIM. After that, we’ll verify service returns. In parallel, I’d like to identify your account so I can rule out any line-side issues.",
  "steps_for_you": [
    "Turn OFF Airplane Mode: Use toggle_airplane_mode to switch Airplane Mode OFF.",
    "Unlock the SIM: When the phone prompts for the SIM PIN, enter your SIM PIN carefully.",
    "Verify service: After unlocking, wait ~30–60 seconds. Then run check_status_bar and check_network_status and share the results (signal strength, network type like 5G/4G, and whether calls/data work)."
  ],
  "important_notes": [
    "About the SIM PIN: Most SIMs allow only about 3 attempts. If you’re unsure of the PIN, do NOT guess. Tell me instead so I can get you the correct next step. Entering it incorrectly too many times will require a PUK code.",
    "If the phone says “PUK required” or “SIM blocked,” stop and tell me immediately—I'll escalate to provide a PUK."
  ],
  "parallel_request_for_account_check": {
    "reason": "If Airplane Mode and SIM unlock don’t fully restore service, I’ll check for any suspension or account-side issues.",
    "please_provide_one_of": [
      "The phone number of the affected line (preferred)",
      "OR your customer ID",
      "OR your full name AND date of birth (YYYY-MM-DD)"
    ]
  },
  "what_to_reply_back_with": [
    "Did Airplane Mode turn OFF successfully?",
    "Were you able to unlock the SIM? If yes, what happened next? If not, what message do you see (e.g., incorrect PIN, PUK required)?",
    "Results of check_status_bar and check_network_status after the above steps."
  ]
}

