messages.content:
{
  "message": "Good news: your SIM is now detected and your line is Active on our side. That means we’re very close—your phone just isn’t attaching to a nearby tower yet. We’ll force a fresh registration and fix any network/APN setting that could block it. None of these steps will erase photos or messages.",
  "thought_process": "Since SIM status is Active, the remaining likely causes are (1) the phone is stuck trying a band that’s not available right now, or (2) APN settings need a reset. We’ll first force a re-attach by switching network modes, then reset APN and reboot if needed. As a temporary backup, Wi‑Fi Calling can get you calling over Wi‑Fi while we finish.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Force a fresh tower attach by switching network modes",
      "do_this": [
        "Go to Settings > Network/Cellular > Preferred network type.",
        "Change it from 4G/5G preferred to 4G/LTE only (or LTE). Wait 60–90 seconds to see if any bars or LTE show up.",
        "Then switch it back to 4G/5G preferred. Wait another 60–90 seconds."
      ],
      "why": "This forces the phone to re-register on a different radio mode, which often restores service when 5G attach is stuck."
    },
    {
      "title": "Reset APN to default, then restart",
      "do_this": [
        "Settings > Mobile Network > Access Point Names (APN) > menu > Reset to default.",
        "Restart the phone once after resetting APN.",
        "After the reboot, wait up to 2 minutes and check for bars/4G/5G."
      ],
      "why": "If APN settings were off, the device may fail to attach properly. Resetting restores carrier defaults."
    },
    {
      "title": "Enable Wi‑Fi Calling (optional, for immediate calling over Wi‑Fi)",
      "do_this": [
        "If you’re on Wi‑Fi, turn on Wi‑Fi Calling: Settings > Cellular/Mobile Network > Wi‑Fi Calling > ON.",
        "This lets you place/receive calls over Wi‑Fi while we finish troubleshooting cellular attach."
      ],
      "why": "Gives you calling ability right now, even if bars haven’t appeared yet."
    }
  ],
  "what_i_need_from_you": [
    "Please do Step 1 now (switch to 4G/LTE only, wait, then back to 4G/5G preferred) and tell me if any bars or network type appears.",
    "If still No Service, please do Step 2 (Reset APN to default and restart) and let me know what you see after the reboot."
  ],
  "next_if_not_resolved": "If these steps don’t restore service, I’ll escalate to a human agent to check for a local tower issue or refresh your network provisioning. I’ll summarize everything we’ve tried so you don’t have to repeat yourself.",
  "reassurance": "You will be able to use your phone again. With SIM and line both active, one of these steps or a quick network-side refresh will bring service back."
}

