  "message": "Thanks for the thorough updates. You now have excellent 5G data and your APN includes an MMSC, so the remaining likely blockers are the messaging app’s permissions/data access or a SIM/session glitch. We’ll verify and correct app permissions, then refresh the SIM session and retry.",
  "reasoning": "MMS requires: (1) mobile data (you have it), (2) a valid MMSC in the APN (now present), and (3) the messaging app’s ability to access media/SMS and use data in the background. If permissions are fine and MMS still fails, reseating the SIM and retesting on 4G-only can clear residual routing issues.",
  "steps_now_in_order": [
    {
      "step": "Check the messaging app’s effective permissions",
      "how": "On your device, run check_app_permissions(app_name=\"messaging\") and share the results. Also open Settings > Apps > Messages > Permissions and note what’s listed.",
      "why": "We need to confirm whether the ‘storage’ (or Photos/Videos) permission is recognized even if it wasn’t shown before."
    },
    {
      "step": "Force‑grant required permissions",
      "how": [
        "Run grant_app_permission(app_name=\"messaging\", permission=\"storage\").",
        "Run grant_app_permission(app_name=\"messaging\", permission=\"sms\")."
      ],
      "then": "Run can_send_mms() again and share the result.",
      "why": "Some Android builds hide the Storage/Media toggle for the default Messages app. Force‑grant ensures MMS can access attachments."
