messages.content:
{
  "message": "Good news: your mobile data and roaming are now working (since web pages load). That means the MMS issue is likely due to a phone setting specific to MMS. I’ll walk you through a few safe checks. None of these will touch your photos or personal files.",
  "why_these_steps": [
    "MMS needs mobile data (you have it), plus the correct APN MMSC entry, and the messaging app must have Storage and SMS permissions.",
    "Wi‑Fi Calling, Data Saver, or a VPN can interfere with MMS—so we’ll rule those out.",
    "Some phones won’t send MMS over Wi‑Fi, so we’ll test with Wi‑Fi OFF."
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Confirm the quick toggles for MMS",
      "instructions": [
        "Turn Wi‑Fi OFF (for testing MMS).",
        "Wi‑Fi Calling OFF: Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Wi‑Fi Calling > OFF.",
        "Data Saver OFF: Settings > Network & Internet > Data Saver > OFF.",
        "VPN OFF: Settings > Network & Internet > VPN > Disconnect any active VPN."
      ],
      "why": "Ensures MMS uses mobile data without interference."
    },
    {
      "title": "Ensure your phone prefers fast networks",
      "instructions": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network > Preferred network type > select 4G/5G."
      ],
      "why": "MMS doesn’t work well on old 2G/3G modes."
    },
    {
      "title": "Check the Messages app permissions and data access",
      "instructions": [
        "Settings > Apps > Messages (or your texting app) > Permissions > Allow: SMS and Storage (Photos/Media/Files).",
        "Still in the app settings, find Mobile data & Wi‑Fi (or Data usage) > ensure Mobile data is allowed and Background data is ON."
      ],
      "why": "The app needs SMS + Storage permission and data access to send pictures."
    },
    {
      "title": "Verify APN has an MMSC entry",
      "instructions": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network > Access Point Names (APN).",
        "Tap the active APN (the one with the dot/checkbox).",
        "Scroll and look for MMSC. Confirm it is filled in (not blank or ‘Not set’).",
        "If MMSC is missing or blank: In the APN screen, tap the menu (⋮) > Reset to default again, then Restart the phone once more."
      ],
      "why": "MMSC is required for MMS. Resetting APN restores the correct MMS server settings."
    },
    {
      "title": "Test MMS",
      "instructions": [
        "With Wi‑Fi OFF and Mobile Data + Data Roaming ON, open Messages and send a small picture (you can try sending it to yourself)."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    "Is Wi‑Fi Calling OFF, Data Saver OFF, and any VPN disconnected?",
    "In Messages app settings, did you grant SMS and Storage permissions and allow background data?",
    "In the APN details, is MMSC filled in? If it was blank, did you reset APN again and reboot?",
    "After these checks, does the picture message send?"
  ],
  "next_step_if_still_failing": "If MMS still won’t send after confirming these items (especially MMSC present and app permissions granted), I can transfer you to a human agent to dig deeper. Just say the word and I’ll initiate the transfer.",
  "reassurance": "All steps above are safe and will not affect your photos or personal data. I’m here with you—tell me what you find on the APN MMSC field and the permissions, and we’ll go from there."
}

